Package: pyramid_chart
Title: Stata Module to Generate a Population Pyramid Chart
Version: 1.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Masud", "Rahman", email = "write2masud@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Fernando", "Rios-Avila", role = "ctb")
  )
Description: A Stata command that draws a population pyramid: back-to-back
    horizontal bars showing the percentage distribution of a numeric variable
    across the levels of one categorical variable, split by a two-level
    categorical variable. Axes, legend and bar labels are built from value
    labels, and any 'twoway' option can be passed through. This DESCRIPTION
    file exists only to build the documentation website with 'pkgdown'; the
    package itself is Stata code, installed with 'ssc install pyramid_chart'.
